CM k9ay-shaped NT probe, IMAGE-TAG form (momwire#456 phase C): the cell
CM structure, with the NT addressing tags 3 and 4 -- wires that exist only
CM because the GX generated them, and that lie OUTSIDE the cell.  An LD
CM written this way is silently DROPPED by NEC and refused by this dialect
CM (see k9ay_orig.deck's rule).  A network card is not: nec2c resolves it
CM against the fully generated structure, attaches it, and answers
CM 55.036 + j497.78 -- no drop, no diagnostic, no error.  This deck is what
CM says network endpoint resolution must see the IMAGES, not just the cell.
CE
GW 1 8 0. 0. 8.5 5. 0. 1.5 1.5E-3
GW 2 5 0. 0. 0. 5. 0. 1.5 1.5E-3
GX 2 100
GE 0
EX 0 4 1 0 1. 0.
NT 3 4 4 3 0.02 0. -0.02 0. 0.02 0.
FR 0 1 0 0 1.8 0
XQ
NX
